ct rule gives\n\n$$\np = \\pm \\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstitution in the original equation confirms each listed root."] [:db/cas 17592186069222 :question/worked-solution nil "Move every term to the left, combine like terms, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{9}{4}=\\frac{\\left(t - 3\\right) \\left(t + 3\\right)}{4}=0.\n$$\n\nThe zero-product rule gives\n\n$$\nt = \\pm 3.\n$$\n\nSubstitution in the original equation confirms each listed root."] [:db/cas 17592186069263 :question/worked-solution nil "Move every term to the left, combine like terms, and factor:\n\n$$\n2 x^{2} - 32=2 \\left(x - 4\\right) \\left(x + 4\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nThe zero-product rule gives\n\n$$\nx = \\pm 4.\n$$\n\nSubstitution in the original equation confirms each listed root."] [:db/cas 17592186069340 :question/worked-solution nil "Move every term to the left, combine like terms, and factor:\n\n$$\nq^{2} - 25=1 \\left(q + 5\\right) \\left(q - 5\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nThe zero-product rule gives\n\n$$\nq = \\pm 5.\n$$\n\nSubstitution in the original equation confirms each listed root."] [:db/cas 17592186069341 :question/worked-solution nil "Move every term to the left, combine like terms, and factor:\n\n$$\n9 y^{2} - 16=9 \\left(y - \\frac{4}{3}\\right) \\left(y + \\frac{4}{3}\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nThe zero-product rule gives\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstitution in the original equation confirms each listed root."] [:db/cas 17592186097099 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int 3 e^{- 6 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}e^{-6x} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 6 x}}{2}+C\\right)=3 e^{- 6 x}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097154 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=- x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097162 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}{\\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\right)=\\frac{10 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097220 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{6 x - 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2^{6x - 1}}{6\\ln 2} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2^{6 x - 1}}{6 \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C\\right)=2^{6 x - 1}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097221 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int 3^{- x - 6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{3^{-x - 6}}{\\ln 3} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- \\frac{3^{- x - 6}}{\\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C\\right)=3^{- x - 6}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097244 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=x^{2} \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right) + 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097245 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{3} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{4} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}} + \\frac{1}{x^{4} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097247 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\left(2 x + 2\\right) e^{x}\\right)=\\left(2 x + 2\\right) e^{x} + 2 e^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given point gives\n\n$$\n4.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186097260 :question/worked-solution nil "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(8 x^{3} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=8 x^{3} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 24 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given point gives\n\n$$\n6 \\pi^{2}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184548 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int 12 x^{3} + 5 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x=3x^{4} + \\frac{5x^{2}}{2} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 x^{4} + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2}+C\\right)=12 x^{3} + 5 x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184549 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sqrt{x} - 3\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{3}}}{3} - 3x + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2 x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 3 x+C\\right)=\\sqrt{x} - 3.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184550 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int - 3 x + \\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{3x^{2}}{2} - \\frac{1}{x} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2} - \\frac{1}{x}+C\\right)=- 3 x + \\frac{1}{x^{2}}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184563 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int - \\sqrt{x} + x^{2} + 2\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{3} - 2\\sqrt{x^{3}} + 6x}{3} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- \\frac{2 x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3} + 2 x+C\\right)=- \\sqrt{x} + x^{2} + 2.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184738 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int x^{\\frac{5}{2}} + \\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{5}{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{x^{7}}}{7} - \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{x^{3}}} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2 x^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{7} - \\frac{2}{3 x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}+C\\right)=x^{\\frac{5}{2}} + \\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{5}{2}}}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184739 :question/worked-solution nil "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int \\sqrt[5]{x} + 4 x^{7} - \\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{13}{7}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{8}}{2} + \\frac{5\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}{6} + \\frac{7}{6\\sqrt[7]{x^{6}}} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5 x^{\\frac{6}{5}}}{6} + \\frac{x^{8}}{2} + \\frac{7}{6 x^{\\frac{6}{7}}}+C\\right)=\\sqrt[5]{x} + 4 x^{7} - \\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{13}{7}}}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186172565 :question/worked-solution nil "Substitute each marked point into $y′=2-xy$. The slopes at $(-1,2)$, $(1,3)$, and $(0,-2)$ are respectively $4,-1,2$. Select the diagram with a steep positive segment on the left, a negative segment at $(1,3)$, and a positive segment at $(0,-2)$."] [:db/cas 17592186172600 :question/worked-solution nil "Substitute each marked point into $y′=x^2-2y$. The slopes at $(1,2)$, $(-1,-1)$, and $(2,-2)$ are respectively $-3,3,8$. Select the diagram with those signed segment slopes."] [:db/cas 17592186172641 :question/worked-solution nil "Compare segments across each horizontal row. In the selected diagram every segment in a row has the same slope, so the slope depends only on $y$. It therefore cannot represent the stated dependence on both $x$ and $y$."] [:db/cas 17592186115777 :question/worked-solution nil "Downward is positive. Gravity is $80g$ and drag is $-kv$. Newton’s law gives $80v′=80g-kv$, hence $v′+(k/80)v=g$."] [:db/cas 17592186115778 :question/worked-solution nil "Downward is positive, so $72v′=72g-18v$. Divide by $72$ to obtain $v′+\\frac14v=g$."] [:db/cas 17592186115779 :question/worked-solution nil "Newton’s law gives $v′+(k/12)v=9.8$. Using $v=9$ and $v′=6.8$ yields $6.8+9k/12=9.8$, so $k=4\\,\\mathrm{kg/s}$. Substitution gives $v′+\\frac13v=g$."] [:db/cas 17592186115780 :question/worked-solution nil "With negligible drag, gravity is the only force. Newton’s law is $mv′=mg$, so $v′=g$."] [:db/cas 17592186147765 :question/worked-solution nil "Write the equation as $(2+ye^{xy})\\,\\mathrm{d}x+(xe^{xy}-2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0$. A potential is $F=e^{xy}-y^2+2x$, since $F_x=2+ye^{xy}$ and $F_y=xe^{xy}-2y$. Thus $e^{xy}-y^2+2x=c$."] [:db/cas 17592186147766 :question/worked-solution nil "The exactness criterion is $P_y=Q_x$. Here $P=2+ye^{xy}$ and $Q=xe^{xy}-2y$, so both partial derivatives equal $e^{xy}+xye^{xy}$. Thus the equation is exact."] [:db/cas 17592186147769 :question/worked-solution nil "The exactness criterion is $P_y=Q_x$. Here $P_y=(2y+xy^2)e^{xy}$, whereas $Q_x=(1+xy)e^{xy}$. They are not identically equal, so the equation is not exact."] [:db/cas 17592186148118 :question/worked-solution nil "Exactness requires $P_y=Q_x$. Since $Q=2y+x$, we have $Q_x=1$. For candidates I, II, III, $P_y$ is respectively $1,1,0$. Therefore I and II only are possible."] [:db/cas 17592186176355 :question/worked-solution nil "Cosine has period $2\\pi$ and is even. Therefore $\\cos(-x+16\\pi)=\\cos(-x)=\\cos x=-11/24$."] [:db/cas 17592186176546 :question/worked-solution nil "Cosine has period $2\\pi$, so $\\cos(x-6\\pi)=\\cos x$. Hence $4\\cos(x-6\\pi)-1=4(\\sqrt3/2)-1=2\\sqrt3-1$."] [:db/cas 17592186176547 :question/worked-solution nil "The shift $10\\pi$ is five full periods, so $\\cos(x+10\\pi)=\\cos x=-1/\\sqrt3$."] [:db/cas 17592186179925 :question/worked-solution nil "At one half-life $H$, $e^{-0.53319H}=1/2$. Thus $H=\\ln2/0.53319=1.3000\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{s}$, which rounds to $1.3\\,\\mathrm{s}$."] [:db/cas 17592186179926 :question/worked-solution nil "Exponential decay gives $M(t)=M_0\\,2^{-t/H}$. At the stated time, $t/H=1.5$, so $M=100\\,2^{-1.5}=35.3553\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{pg}$, or $35.36\\,\\mathrm{pg}$."] [:db/cas 17592186179927 :question/worked-solution nil "The remaining fraction is $0.15=2^{-t/717000}$. Taking logarithms gives $t=717000\\ln(1/0.15)/\\ln2=1962404\\ldots$ years, approximately $1$ million $962$ thousand years."] [:db/cas 17592186180079 :question/worked-solution nil "The remaining fraction is $6.25/200=1/32=(1/2)^5$. Five half-lives have elapsed, so $t=5(15.2)=76\\,\\mathrm{s}$."] [:db/cas 17592186180080 :question/worked-solution nil "At the half-life, $e^{-0.001k}=1/2$. Therefore $k=\\ln2/0.001=693.147\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$, which is $693$ to three significant figures."] [:db/cas 17592186229692 :question/worked-solution nil "Substitute $t=0$ into the stated model $Q(t)=\\alpha+\\beta e^{-kt}$. Since $e^0=1$ and the initial salt mass is $6\\,\\mathrm{kg}$, $\\alpha+\\beta=Q(0)=6$."] [:db/cas 17592186229694 :question/worked-solution nil "The volume is $V(t)=120+(9-6)t=120+3t$. Overflow begins when $V=210$, so $t=30\\,\\mathrm{min}$. Mass balance gives $Q′=4.5-6Q/(120+3t)$. Its solution satisfying $Q(0)=30$ is $Q=\\frac12(120+3t)-30(120/(120+3t))^2$. At $t=30$, $Q=95.204\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{lb}$, hence $95.2\\,\\mathrm{lb}$."] [:db/cas 17592186229725 :question/worked-solution nil "The volume stays $900\\,\\mathrm{L}$. The salt inflow is $0.02(30)=0.6\\,\\mathrm{kg/min}$ and outflow is $30Q/900=Q/30$. Thus $Q′+Q/30=0.6$. With $Q(0)=10$, $Q(t)=18-8e^{-t/30}$. Consequently $Q(6)=11.4501\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{kg}$, or $11.45\\,\\mathrm{kg}$."] [:db/cas 17592186064554 :question/problem "Calculate $\\intxdx$." "Calculate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186064556 :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx^{4}dx$." "Calculate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int x^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186594690 :question/worked-solution "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K.\n$$\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{′}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4t}{{t}^{2}+1})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({t}^{2}+3)^{2})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+3)^{2}}\\right)+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "In part 9, we found that\n\n$$\n-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K.\n$$\n\nSince $t>0$, we have $\\ln|t|=\\ln t$. Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function in the partial sum decomposition of ${y}^{′}(t)$ found in part 8:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4t}{{t}^{2}+3})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-4\\int \\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+3)+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({t}^{2}+3)^{2})+K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+3)^{2}}\\right)+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186363774 :question/problem "A sealed medical courier capsule of mass $9\\,\\text{kg}$ is released from rest with an initial downward velocity of $4.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Let $v(t)$ be the capsule's velocity, in meters per second, $t\\ge 0$ seconds after release, with downward taken as the positive direction. The air resistance acting on the capsule is negligible, and the only other force acting on it is its weight due to gravity.\n\nFind the equation for $v(t).$ Express your answer in terms of time $t$ and acceleration due to gravity $g.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "A sealed medical courier capsule of mass $9\\,\\text{kg}$ is launched downward with an initial velocity of $4.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Let $v(t)$ be the capsule's velocity, in meters per second, $t\\ge 0$ seconds after release, with downward taken as the positive direction. The air resistance acting on the capsule is negligible, and the only other force acting on it is its weight due to gravity.\n\nFind the equation for $v(t).$ Express your answer in terms of time $t$ and acceleration due to gravity $g.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186147766 :question/problem "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n$(2 + ye^{xy})dx + (xe^{xy} - 2y)dy = 0$A differential equation of the form\n\n$P(x, y)dx + Q(x, y)dy = 0$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂x} = \\frac{∂Q}{∂y}$ {{field-1}}" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n(2+ye^{xy})\\,\\mathrm{d}x+(xe^{xy}-2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nTo test whether it is exact, write it as $P(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0$. Which partial-derivative equality is the exactness criterion?\n\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186147769 :question/problem "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n$(2 + y^{2}e^{xy})dx + (xe^{xy} - 2y)dy = 0$A differential equation of the form\n\n$P(x, y)dx + Q(x, y)dy = 0$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂x} = \\frac{∂Q}{∂y}$ {{field-1}}" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n(2+y^2e^{xy})\\,\\mathrm{d}x+(xe^{xy}-2y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nTo test whether it is exact, write it as $P(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0$. Which partial-derivative equality is the exactness criterion?\n\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186235391 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\n$$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." "$$\n\\int y^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\ln({{field-1}})+K,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/cas 17592186594690 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\n$${{field-1}}\n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." "$$\n\\int y^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\ln({{field-1}})+K,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/cas 17592186601926 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int {y}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\n$${{field-1}}\n$)+\\,K,$\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant." "$$\n\\int y^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\ln({{field-1}})+K,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/cas 17592186677832 :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int \\sqrt[4]{t}-t^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t>0$." "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int \\sqrt[4]{t}-t^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t>0$."] [:db/cas 17592186677834 :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int -t^{2}-\\sqrt[4]{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t>0$." "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -t^{2}-\\sqrt[4]{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t>0$."] [:db/cas 17592186681140 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -6\\sqrt{t}-4t^{2}-3\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. Assume $t>0$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -6\\sqrt{t}-4t^{2}-3\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\n. Assume $t>0$."] [:db/cas 17592186694428 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -6+x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -6+x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694436 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -y^{3}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}y$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -y^{3}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694450 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x^{4}+1\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int x^{4}+1\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694457 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -t^{4}+2\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -t^{4}+2\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694460 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x^{3}+4\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int x^{3}+4\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694585 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -1+x-3x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -1+x-3x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694590 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int 3+t-t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 3+t-t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694596 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -3-3x-2x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -3-3x-2x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186694602 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int -3-2t^{2}+2t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." "Calculate \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int -3-2t^{2}+2t\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186704829 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant of integration.\n\n{{antiderivative